      "id": "sol.amc-8-2019-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Recall that \\[a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b).\\] We can do the following rearrangement. \\[ \\begin{aligned} (x^2 - 5)^2 - 4^2 &= 0 \\\\ (x^2 - 1)(x^2 - 9) &= 0 \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nFrom this we can see that there are \\(4\\) possible values for \\(x.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
